"""Review head collision detail budgets and the simplified rear support."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
from survey import ROOT,OUT

def main():
    renders=json.loads((OUT/'renders.json').read_text());geometry=json.loads((OUT/'geometry-verification.json').read_text());data={}
    for item in json.loads((OUT/'variants.json').read_text()):
        r=json.loads(Path(item['path']).read_text());key=r['variant'];views={}
        for row in renders['views']:
            if row['variant']==key:views.setdefault(row['scope'],{}).setdefault(row['camera'],{})[row['stage']]=row['path']
        proof=next(x for x in geometry['variants']if x['variant']==key)
        data[key]=dict(views=views,headBefore=r['source_head_triangles'],headAfter=r['candidate_head_triangles'],saving=r['placed_mesh_saving'],
            removed=len(r['omitted_collision_owners']),nativeField=r['field_native_mesh_triangles'],previewField=r['field_preview_triangles'],rays=proof['interface_first_hit_rays']['probes'])
    html='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><style>
body{font-family:var(--font-sans,system-ui);color:var(--foreground);line-height:1.45}p{margin:0 0 12px}.muted,small{color:var(--muted-foreground)}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:14px 0}select{font:inherit;color:var(--foreground);background:var(--background);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:7px;padding:8px;max-width:100%}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px}.caption{font-size:13px;margin-bottom:5px}.imagebox{aspect-ratio:1;background:#c3d2e0;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden}.imagebox img{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px;margin:14px 0}td,th{text-align:left;padding:8px 5px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.note{padding:16px;margin:14px 0;background:var(--secondary);border-radius:var(--radius,10px)}.note p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}small{font-size:12px}
</style></head><body>
<p><strong>The head is the next useful target.</strong> This first collision trial removes compact neutral detail outside the tool interface and rebuilds the rear support. Approved visuals stay byte-identical.</p>
<div class="controls"><select id="variant" aria-label="Detail budget"><option value="compact-12mm">12 mm compact detail budget</option><option value="compact-8mm">8 mm conservative budget</option></select><select id="reference" aria-label="Reference"><option value="current">Current collision</option><option value="visual">Approved visual appearance</option></select><select id="scope" aria-label="Scope"><option value="head">Whole head</option><option value="cutaway">Collision cutaway</option><option value="rear-support">Rear support close-up</option><option value="whole-core">Whole Core</option></select><select id="camera" aria-label="Camera"><option value="back">Back</option><option value="front">Front</option><option value="left">Side</option></select></div>
<div class="pair"><div><p class="caption" id="beforeLabel"></p><div class="imagebox"><img id="before" alt="Current head reference"></div></div><div><p class="caption">Head collision candidate</p><div class="imagebox"><img id="after" alt="Simplified head collision"></div></div></div>
<p class="muted" style="font-size:13px;margin-top:9px">Orange: collision detail selected for omission. Blue: rebuilt rear support. Grey: retained collision. The cutaway hides the same enclosing panels on both sides.</p>
<table><tbody><tr><td>Head collision triangles per Core</td><td>37,574 → <strong id="headAfter"></strong></td></tr><tr><td>Triangles saved across both Cores</td><td><strong id="saving"></strong></td></tr><tr><td>Compact collision owners omitted per Core</td><td id="removed"></td></tr></tbody></table>
<div class="note"><p><strong>The front tool interface is retained.</strong> The slotted front, colored/white panels, threaded sleeve and named central tool parts keep their source arrays. All <span id="rays"></span> sampled front-interface rays keep exactly the same first hit.</p><p>The rear support becomes seven box-shaped mesh volumes: 1,262 → 84 triangles per Core. It retains the 76.2 mm rail spacing and 50 × 30 mm central recess. Its small channels and holes close; sampled source protrusions extend up to 2.53 mm outside the solids, and new surfaces can be 20 mm from the old detail.</p></div>
<p><strong>What remains in the arm:</strong> 3,354 mesh triangles per Core. The 1,090-triangle squared connector is the largest remaining piece; its cylinder trial was rejected. The head therefore offers larger gains.</p>
<p class="muted"><small>These are collision omissions, not visual deletions. “12 mm” is a maximum source bounding-box span for selected neutral parts, not an error bound; their source names do not prove every part is a screw. Every compact owner overlapping the central tool-interface rectangle is retained. No all-pose/contact or speedup approval follows from the ray grid.</small></p>
<p class="muted"><small id="field"></small></p><p class="muted"><small>Both head variants remain uninstalled and uncommitted. All 39 approved arm/base cylinders per Core remain exact. The new rear boxes are still triangle meshes; native box import is separate work. Matched views use diagnostic flat lighting.</small></p>
<script>const data=__DATA__,el=id=>document.getElementById(id);function show(){let d=data[el('variant').value],r=el('reference').value,s=el('scope').value,c=el('camera').value,v=d.views[s][c];el('before').src=v[r];el('after').src=v.candidate;el('beforeLabel').textContent=el('reference').selectedOptions[0].textContent;for(let k of ['headAfter','saving','removed','rays'])el(k).textContent=d[k].toLocaleString();el('field').textContent='Whole-field trial: 344,792 visual triangles unchanged; collision is either '+d.previewField.toLocaleString()+' diagnostic mesh triangles or '+d.nativeField.toLocaleString()+' remaining mesh triangles + 78 native cylinders. These alternatives are counted separately.';}['variant','reference','scope','camera'].forEach(id=>el(id).onchange=show);show();console.log('Head collision review: two variants, 72 matched images');</script>
</body></html>'''
    (OUT/'gallery.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data)))

if __name__=='__main__':main()
